Detection Logic

Credential attacks are commonly detected by identifying high volumes of failed authentication attempts from a single source IP.

Example Splunk detection query:

index=windows EventCode=4625
| stats count by src_ip TargetUserName
| where count > 50
| sort -count

This query identifies abnormal authentication volumes that may indicate password spraying or credential stuffing.

