Findings

The investigation confirmed:

3,227 failed authentication attempts

Targeting of multiple local accounts

2 NTLM network logons (LogonType 3)

No interactive sessions

No privilege escalation

No process execution

No persistence mechanisms

No lateral movement activity

Conclusion

The activity is consistent with automated credential validation attempts, commonly associated with password spraying or credential stuffing attacks.

Although two NTLM network authentications succeeded, the investigation found no evidence of post-authentication exploitation or compromise.

Security Recommendations

Review external exposure of NTLM authentication

Strengthen local administrator credentials

Implement account lockout policies

Monitor abnormal authentication volumes

Enforce strong password policies

